---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI-generated content - theJugglingCompany.com"
  description="How this site uses AI-generated images, and how they are labelled, in line with the EU AI Act."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 md:px-6 lg:px-10">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-muted)]">
      Transparency
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-5xl">
      AI-generated content
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[var(--color-muted)]">
      In line with the EU AI Act (Article 50) transparency rules, this page explains
      which imagery on the site is AI-generated and how it is marked.
    </p>

    <div class="prose mt-12">
      <h2>What is AI-generated</h2>
      <p>
        Most illustrative and decorative images on this site - the abstract renders
        of hands, balls, light trails, neural and infinity motifs, and similar
        conceptual artwork - are generated with AI image tools. Wherever one of
        these images appears, it carries a small <strong>"AI-generated"</strong> badge.
        Some AI-generated pieces also keep their original NotebookLM watermark.
      </p>

      <h2>What is not AI-generated</h2>
      <p>These are real, and are never labelled as AI:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Photographs of Linda</strong> - real photos from stages, conferences, and practice.</li>
        <li><strong>Screenshots</strong> - genuine captures of code editors, dashboards, and detection results.</li>
        <li><strong>Videos on the linked YouTube channel</strong> - real recordings, not AI.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to tell the difference</h2>
      <p>
        AI-generated images show the "AI-generated" badge in the corner of the image.
        If an image has no badge, it is a real photograph, screenshot, or video still.
      </p>

      <h2>The writing</h2>
      <p>
        Every article on this site starts as my own thinking, built on more than a
        decade of juggling and the experiences behind it. I use AI as a tool - to
        tighten the writing, to research, and sometimes to summarise studies or
        articles - but the ideas, the juggling experience, and the judgement are
        mine. I know the material I write about first-hand, and I have travelled to
        every country mentioned on the site.
      </p>
      <p>
        One honest exception: the juggling-shops directory. The only shop I have
        personally visited is here in Vienna. The rest is a directory I maintain to
        help jugglers find gear worldwide - I welcome reviews and support from the
        community, and I will add my own as I visit more shops while travelling.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If anything here is unclear or looks mislabelled, get in touch at
        <a href="mailto:hello@lindamohamed.com">hello@lindamohamed.com</a> and it will be corrected.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
